# Visual Enhancements Walkthrough

This walkthrough documents the visual enhancements made to the game, including increased floor fire sprite size, collision particle effects, and a full-width enemy health bar.

## Changes Made

### 1. Increased Floor Fire Sprite Size

**File Modified:** [floor_fire.dart](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/floor_fire.dart#L37-L39)

The floor fire sprite size was increased from 15% to 25% of the screen height for better visibility:

```diff
-    // Size it appropriately
-    double newHeight = game.size.y * 0.15;
+    // Size it appropriately - increased from 0.15 to 0.25 for better visibility
+    double newHeight = game.size.y * 0.25;
     double newWidth = (spriteSize.x / spriteSize.y) * newHeight;
     size = Vector2(newWidth, newHeight);
```

**Impact:** The floor fire hazards in Level 2 are now 66% larger and much easier to see.

---

### 2. Collision Particle Effects

**New File Created:** [collision_particle.dart](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/collision_particle.dart)

Created a new particle system that spawns animated particles when collisions occur:

- **Particle Behavior:** 8 particles per collision that spread out in all directions
- **Animation:** Particles fade out over 0.5 seconds with gravity and deceleration effects
- **Configurable:** Color, lifetime, and particle count can be customized

**Integration:**

#### Enemy Collision Particles (Orange)
**File Modified:** [enemy.dart](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/enemy.dart#L109-L117)

When a player bullet hits an enemy, orange particles spawn:

```dart
// Spawn collision particles
final particle = CollisionParticle(
  position: position.clone(),
  color: const Color(0xFFFF6600), // Orange particles for enemy damage
);
game.add(particle);
```

#### Player Collision Particles (Green)
**File Modified:** [player.dart](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/player.dart#L111-L119)

When an enemy bullet hits the player, green particles spawn:

```dart
// Spawn collision particles for player damage
final particle = CollisionParticle(
  position: position.clone(),
  color: const Color(0xFF00FF00), // Green particles for player damage
);
game.add(particle);
```

**Impact:** Collisions now have clear visual feedback with color-coded particles:
- 🟠 **Orange** = Enemy taking damage
- 🟢 **Green** = Player taking damage

---

### 3. Full-Width Enemy Health Bar

**File Modified:** [enemy.dart](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/enemy.dart#L57-L58)

Removed the small health bar that appeared above the enemy sprite.

**File Modified:** [battle_game.dart](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/battle_game.dart#L35-L97)

Added a new full-width health bar at the top of the screen with:

- ⬛ **Dark gray background** across the full width (with padding)
- 🟥➡️🟩 **Color gradient** from red (low health) to green (full health)  
- ⬜ **White border** around the health bar
- 📊 **Health text** displaying "current / max" health centered in the bar

```dart
// Render enemy health bar at top of screen (full width)
const barHeight = 30.0;
const barTop = 20.0;
const sidePadding = 20.0;
final barWidth = size.x - (sidePadding * 2);

// Health bar background (dark gray)
final backgroundRect = Rect.fromLTWH(sidePadding, barTop, barWidth, barHeight);
paint.color = const Color(0xFF333333);
canvas.drawRect(backgroundRect, paint);

// Health bar foreground (gradient from red to green)
final healthRect = Rect.fromLTWH(
  sidePadding,
  barTop,
  barWidth * healthPercentage,
  barHeight,
);
final healthColor = Color.lerp(
  const Color(0xFFFF0000), // Red
  const Color(0xFF00FF00), // Green
  healthPercentage,
);
paint.color = healthColor!;
canvas.drawRect(healthRect, paint);

// Border and health text...
```

**Impact:** Enemy health is now clearly visible at all times at the top of the screen, making it much easier to track battle progress.

---

## Summary

All three enhancements have been successfully implemented:

✅ **Floor fire sprites** are now 66% larger (25% vs 15% of screen height)  
✅ **Collision particles** provide instant visual feedback with color-coded effects  
✅ **Enemy health bar** spans the full width of the screen at the top with health percentage display  

These changes apply to both Level 1 and Level 2 battles, as [BattleGameLevel2](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/battle_game_lvl2.dart#7-56) inherits from [BattleGame](file:///c:/Users/bryal/Android/juego/LastCommit/bvst/lib/game/battle_game.dart#7-54).

## Testing

To test these changes, run the game and:

1. Navigate to Level 1 or Level 2 battle
2. Observe the **larger floor fire sprites** in Level 2
3. Shoot the enemy and watch for **orange particle effects**
4. Get hit by enemy bullets and watch for **green particle effects**
5. Check the **full-width health bar** at the top of the screen as you damage the enemy

```bash
cd c:\Users\bryal\Android\juego\LastCommit\bvst
flutter run
```
